ause]  thank you  you'll let me know what you think down  in the comments section below keep in  mind I am recording through a lav mic  and this is going online but what I can  hear personally is that this is a tough  call so the surface laptop 3 is  definitely a little bit louder judging  off of my Apple watch it peaked about  one decibel louder and you can tell that  it also has a little bit more bass and  then the high frequencies all are a  little bit more kind of sharp whereas  the MacBook Pro is more balanced and the  mates have more clarity if I had to  choose one to live with I would probably  say I would rather have a little bit  more loudness even though the overall  sound quality might be a little bit  worse just because in certain  environments that can be really useful  now it's time to get into performance  both these laptops are using Intel's  latest 10 nanometer I 5 quad-core  processors 8 gigabytes of low power ddr4  memory and they both use Intel iris + g7  graphics which are a great deal at this  price point compared to a lot of the  competition so this is going to get  interesting I'm gonna go ahead and start  the CPU benchmark the MacBook Air has a  1.1 gigahertz base goes up to 3.5  compared to a 1.5 that goes up to 3.7 so  surface laptop 3 I believe it uses the u  processor and whereas the MacBook Air  uses a Y processor and that just means  that the MacBook Air is designed to save  more power be more power efficient and  we're gonna talk about battery life in  just a bit as well and here's our  results not only does the surface laptop  3 beat the MacBook Air in single core  performance by just a little bit with a  very excellent score in multi-core it's  actually about 35% more powerful and not  as pod just because of the extra wattage  that it can use for the CPU now let's go  ahead and test out graphics it looks  like the surface laptop 3 gets about a  20% higher score in terms of graphics  and I wanted to do a gaming test here  but unfortu