y way  the MacBook Air can keep itself cool  enough without shutting down is by  slowing down the chip if we had better  cooling maybe there'd only be about a  15% difference instead of what we are  seeing I know a lot of you guys asked  for SSD tests so here we go we're gonna  start both of these and we're seeing a  pretty big difference  Apple's SSD in terms of write speed is a  lot faster as far as the read comparison  so the surface laptop is just a sliver  faster basically the same at 1400 but  the MacBook Air  is close to three times as fast for the  right speeds so we compared a bunch of  different areas but what about pricing  and value well the MacBook Pro  surprisingly if we're just looking at  MSRP z' is about $200 cheaper with the  same amount of RAM SSD storage and also  an i-5 quad-core processor but with that  said you can get some great deals on the  surface laptop three I'll go ahead and  have a link in the video description to  Amazon where you can get 300 bucks off  of this laptop and that brings these two  much closer together it makes us  actually a little bit cheaper now as I  mentioned it's a very tough choice with  the surface laptop 3 you're gonna have  better performance especially under  extended load for both CPU and graphics  and that could be great the screens a  little bit taller which is nice for  productivity on such a small device and  in general it is an excellent laptop  where the MacBook Air really shines is  Mac OS I definitely notice using both of  these that the MacBook Air is snappier  opening up programs web browsing  unzipping files doing downloads  everything feels snappier and I don't  have as much issues as far as crashes  and apps not working for example I  really wanted to run the unit in heaven  I could not get it to work  there's just errors like this and on top  of that we do have a difference in  battery life the MacBook Air gets about  two to three hours better battery life  and mixed uses and we also have  Thunde